qx|A3|st||rh||ah|Board 3 IMPs   -   January 24, 2024|pn|hondo717,IraCT,danpsych,toasterln|
md|1S974H653DAQ6CA863,SKQT6HJ9DKT87CQJ5,SA832H72DJ542C742,SJ5HAKQT84D93CKT9|sv|e|
mb|P|mb|P|mb|P|mb|2H|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|The very nice 2@H bid in 4th seat that is NOT a weak 2 bid. There is no point in preempting in 4th seat because you can pass and no need to preempt the opponents. So 2@H, in 4th seat, shows a nice 6-card suit and no more than 13 or 14 points.|
PG| ***** 40 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|3H|mb|P|mb|P|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|3@H is probably invitational and I would bid 4@H with the East hand. On the other hand, one could argue that 3@H is also preemptive and if it is, then pass is correct. In any case I think West should have bid 4@H.|
PG| ***** 41 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^^B@2^*BA Kib: ^*NWhy didn't East open 1@H?|
PG| ***** 42 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^^
^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Because, after three passes, 2@H is a more descriptive bid in 4th seat.|
PG| ***** 43 ***** |


