mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|3H|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|With a 15+ hand, the 3@H is at least a mild slam try and West has a pretty nice hand so should start control bidding.|
PG| ***** 62 ***** |


mb|P|mb|3S|mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|4C|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|East is worried about diamond controls so 4@C is the perfect bid. If West bids 4@H, that denies a diamond control and they stop in game. On this hand West has a diamond control.|
PG| ***** 63 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|4S|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|We are going to play |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=kickback,Kickback^*N|CP||FP||at| RKCB where 4@S is RKCB. It has the advantage of allowing for the queen ask. On this hand, assuming you play 0314, the advantage of |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=kickback,Kickback^*N|CP||FP||at| is demonstrated.|
PG| ***** 64 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|if 4N was RKCB, East would have to bid 5@D (1) and the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=queenask,Queen Ask^*N|CP||FP||at| would not be possible without forcing to slam. But with |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=kickback,Kickback^*N|CP||FP||at|, missing 1 key card West needs to find out if East has the @HQ to determine whether or not to bid 6.|
PG| ***** 65 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|5C|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|5@C is 1 or 4 keycards.|
PG| ***** 66 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|5D|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|That is the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=queenask,Queen Ask^*N|CP||FP||at|. With @HQ East bids the cheapest King or 6@H with no outside King.|
